      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (23%):</strong> Deal fails through June 15 (p≈0.72) and the US exercises the "other options" flagged by Rubio, potentially involving resumed kinetic action against IRGC assets or Iran's nuclear infrastructure, drawing a new round of retaliation.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (52%):</strong> Negotiations extend beyond June 15 without formal collapse or agreement, Hormuz remains at 2-10% of pre-war transit levels, Israeli elections proceed on their own timeline in September-October, and the conflict settles into a frozen deterrence posture.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (25%):</strong> A signed Iran-US framework materializes by 15 June (NF2 p=0.28), Lloyd's re-enters within days, Hormuz commercial traffic rebuilds over the following 3-4 weeks, and the Israeli domestic electoral timeline proceeds decoupled from the Iran track.</p>
